      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFollow-up to #62601, addressing @tomasruizt's review (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/62601#pullrequestreview-5597769386).\n\n- State that the rules in `tests/AGENTS.md` are defaults: an agent may deviate when one does not fit, and must say why in the PR. Weakening a test to make it pass stays forbidden.\n- Add the trade-off between end-to-end tests (robust to refactors, slow) and unit tests on pure functions (fast, partial coverage), and encourage factoring logic into pure functions.\n- Allow mocks for objects that are impractical to construct, with the reason stated in the test.\n- Allow seeded statistical assertions (p-value, confidence interval) when sampling itself (temperature > 0) is under test.\n- In `AGENTS.md`, prefer adding a case to an existing parametrized test, then extending existing tests, before writing a new one.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nDocs-only change. Ran `markdownlint-cli2` with the repo config on both files. Gave fresh agents with no prior context (a Claude subagent and Kimi) four tasks against this checkout: a top-p edge-case fix, a min-p distribution change at temperature 0.8, a helper inside the KV cache manager, and a 1-in-5 CI flake with an `atol` mismatch.\n\n## Test Result\n\n`markdownlint-cli2`: 0 issues. Both agents added a case to the existing sampler test file, used a seeded chi-square test for the sampling change, tested the KV cache helper as a pure function or through the existing real-manager fixtures instead of mocks, and refused to widen `atol`, add reruns, or `xfail` for the flake.\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used to draft this change; the submitter reviewed every changed line.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
