    {
      "additions": 3,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/b852b9bfc91aea45fcb6eec4c31fac4329588c51/AGENTS.md",
      "changes": 5,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/AGENTS.md?ref=b852b9bfc91aea45fcb6eec4c31fac4329588c51",
      "deletions": 2,
      "filename": "AGENTS.md",
      "patch": "@@ -91,8 +91,9 @@ When adding tests:\n   the cheapest level that actually reproduces it? Fixes to user-visible\n   behavior need a test through a real entry point (`LLM`, OpenAI server); see\n   [`tests/AGENTS.md`](tests/AGENTS.md).\n-- **Reuse before create.** Extend existing test files, `conftest.py` fixtures, and\n-  helpers; add a new file only when no nearby suite fits.\n+- **Reuse before create.** First try adding a case to an existing parametrized\n+  test, then extending or refactoring existing tests, `conftest.py` fixtures, and\n+  helpers; add a new test or file only when no nearby suite fits.\n - **Test behavior with intent.** Assert observable outcomes through public APIs;\n   state why in the name or docstring. Skip trivial wiring; flaky tests are worse\n   than no tests.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/b852b9bfc91aea45fcb6eec4c31fac4329588c51/AGENTS.md",
      "sha": "ab2561e8a135c95d1c385fccc1a888561907a142",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 29,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/b852b9bfc91aea45fcb6eec4c31fac4329588c51/tests%2FAGENTS.md",
      "changes": 47,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/tests%2FAGENTS.md?ref=b852b9bfc91aea45fcb6eec4c31fac4329588c51",
      "deletions": 18,
      "filename": "tests/AGENTS.md",
      "patch": "@@ -1,14 +1,22 @@\n # tests\n \n-- **Test real objects on the lightest real path.** Construct vLLM objects with\n-  their real constructors; do not stand them in with `SimpleNamespace` or\n-  `MagicMock`, set private attributes, or patch methods to reach a state. Mock\n-  only external services. Pick the cheapest setup that exercises the change: a\n-  layer or kernel test does not need `vllm_runner`, and single-rank parallel\n-  state is enough when parallelism is irrelevant. A fix to user-visible behavior\n-  needs at least one regression test through `LLM` (`vllm_runner`) or\n-  `RemoteOpenAIServer`, with real weights when loading is involved. A test that\n-  only asserts `assert_called*` or \"no exception\" guards nothing.\n+These are defaults, not absolutes: when one does not fit, deviate and say why in\n+the PR. Never weaken a test to make it pass.\n+\n+- **Choose the level deliberately.** End-to-end tests through `LLM`\n+  (`vllm_runner`) or `RemoteOpenAIServer` survive refactors but take seconds to\n+  minutes; unit tests on pure functions iterate fast but cover only a slice, so\n+  factor complex logic into pure functions where you can. A fix to\n+  user-visible behavior needs at least one end-to-end regression test, with real\n+  weights when loading is involved. A layer or kernel test does not need\n+  `vllm_runner`; single-rank parallel state is enough when parallelism is\n+  irrelevant.\n+- **Prefer real objects.** Construct vLLM objects with their real constructors\n+  rather than `SimpleNamespace` or `MagicMock`, setting private attributes, or\n+  patching methods; such tests couple to the implementation. Mock external\n+  services, or an object that is impractical to construct, and say why in the\n+  test. A test that only asserts `assert_called*` or \"no exception\" guards\n+  nothing.\n - **Show the failure before the fix.** When the bug is reproducible, run the new\n   test on the base commit (rebuild if the fix touches `csrc/`) and confirm it\n   fails for the reported reason, then passes with the fix. Paste both commands\n@@ -20,15 +28,18 @@\n   on main (`.buildkite/scripts/rerun-test.sh`,\n   `docs/contributing/ci/failures.md`); the only exception is\n   `xfail(strict=True)` linking an open issue for a bug on main.\n-- **Deterministic and exact by construction.** Use greedy or seeded sampling.\n-  Assert equality where the result is exact (a change that must not alter\n-  output is compared against the code it replaces, not another reference), and\n-  keep tolerances as tight as the math allows. vLLM is not batch invariant by default: batch size, chunked\n-  prefill, prefix caching, backend, and TP size can flip greedy tokens, so\n-  compare against a reference with `check_logprobs_close` /\n-  `check_embeddings_close`, or require `VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1` for exact\n-  equality. Never synchronize with a fixed `sleep`; poll an explicit condition\n-  with a timeout, and force race orderings with events.\n+- **Deterministic and exact by construction.** Use greedy or seeded sampling;\n+  when the behavior under test is sampling itself (temperature > 0), fix the\n+  seed and assert a statistic against a stated bound (p-value, confidence\n+  interval) rather than exact tokens. Assert equality where the result is exact\n+  (a change that must not alter output is compared against the code it\n+  replaces, not another reference), and keep tolerances as tight as the math\n+  allows. vLLM is not batch invariant by default: batch size, chunked prefill,\n+  prefix caching, backend, and TP size can flip greedy tokens, so compare\n+  against a reference with `check_logprobs_close` / `check_embeddings_close`,\n+  or require `VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1` for exact equality. Never synchronize\n+  with a fixed `sleep`; poll an explicit condition with a timeout, and force\n+  race orderings with events.\n - **Make sure CI runs it.** A test no step in `.buildkite/test_areas/*.yaml`\n   selects never runs, which looks like passing. Check that the step's\n   `commands` and pytest markers (`core_model`, `slow_test`, `distributed`)",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/b852b9bfc91aea45fcb6eec4c31fac4329588c51/tests%2FAGENTS.md",
      "sha": "b8b73dc94a9480676b7876cf0d5975e3ccca12e0",
      "status": "modified"
    }
